        # proved in a unit test.
        "name": "browser_fake",
        "description": (
            "Force a 404, a 500 or a hang on every request whose URL contains `pattern`. This is the "
            "only way to prove 'the board freezes when the API is down' against the REAL app rather "
            "than in a unit test. It is enforced inside the page, in the same fetch and XHR wrappers "
            "the console and network logs already read, so a faked request never touches the network. "
            "Pass clear=true to remove one. A fake left in place is a lie the page keeps believing, so "
            "clear it when you are done — an observation while one is active says so."
        ),
        "inputSchema": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
